/**
 * The universal part of the Technical Knowledge Ledger: zone 1 (metadata-only references to public standards) and zone 2 (Empathia's
 * own explanations, reference cards, worked calculations, decision trees, procedures and failure patterns). Vendor-neutral; no
 * product, maker or customer is named.
 *
 * THE HONEST STATE OF THIS LIBRARY (read before changing REVIEW): every object here was written for the demonstration by an AI
 * system and has been checked only by unit tests, which recompute each worked example. No engineer has reviewed it yet. So each object
 * is IN_REVIEW with no reviewer, and its source carries the weakest authority in the founder's hierarchy (10). The page shows that
 * state on every object and nothing here is presented as fact (contract.ts › isFact). When a named engineer has reviewed the library,
 * change REVIEW below — one place — to that review; nothing else needs to change.
 *
 * Standards are cited by title and number only (zone 1). Their text, tables and clause numbers are not reproduced anywhere here.
 * Where a figure comes from a standard, the object gives the concept and points at the reference. Nothing here asks anyone to work at
 * height, open equipment, touch power or defeat a protection.
 */
